      "id": "nevada-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.leg.state.nv.us/nrs/nrs-236.html",
      "title": "The legal holidays of Nevada (NRS 236.015(1)) that `us-federal-holidays`\ndoes not already close: Nevada Day, observed on the last Friday in\nOctober, and Family Day, the Friday following the fourth Thursday in\nNovember. NRS 236.015(2) closes the courts on them, and FRCP 6(a)(6)(C)\nand FRBP 9006(a)(6)(C) make them legal holidays of the District of Nevada\nfor a period counted forward only (core's `frcp6-nevada` and\n`frbp9006-nevada`). The other (1) days are federal holidays on the same\ndays, observed as (3) and § 6103(b)(1) both observe them.\n\nEach day is closed from the date the vendored text is dated (the\nchapter's revision of April 15, 2026) to the end of 2050. Not modeled:\nOctober 31 itself, which (1) names as Nevada Day but does not observe;\nand the days the President appoints, which no vendored source lists."
    }
